      "writtenOn": "2022-09-09T13:37:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The key doesn\u0027t strictly speaking have to have the exact same block order as the evaluated shader, but it probably clarifies things to keep them consistent. I believe the primitive blender combines the output of the shader (or paint color when there\u0027s no shader) with the primitive color.\n\nThat would suggest it goes below the `if (fShader) {} else {}` block at line 75 below. At that point we have our \"shader\" color set up to be either the SkShader output or the paint color.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "ccb64dc37a9ca034cceb04334ec28e137c5af6b5",
